<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:spiffworkflow="http://spiffworkflow.org/bpmn/schema/1.0/core" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="Definitions_ErrorLogTicketTriage" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn">
  <bpmn:process id="error_log_ticket_triage_process" name="Error Log Ticket Triage" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>Migrated from onefm_mcp's ErrorLogTicketAgent (WI-002204). On every Error Log insert: skip if the kill switch (AI Agent Configuration "Error Log Ticket Agent".enabled) is off, or if the log is the engine's own recursion noise (start condition). Otherwise do a deterministic exact-title dedup against open HD Tickets first — only if that finds nothing does an AI Agent Task judge near-duplicates, returning a structured {decision, ticket_name} so the correct ticket is linked (the old code's bug: it always linked existing_tickets[0] on an AI match, never the ticket the model actually meant). No match -> a new HD Ticket is created with the fields the current Helpdesk schema actually requires (custom_ticket_category is mandatory; custom_is_doctype_related no longer exists).</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="start_error_logged" name="Error Log Created" spiffworkflow:triggerDoctype="Error Log" spiffworkflow:triggerType="After Insert">
      <bpmn:outgoing>f1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:conditionalEventDefinition id="CondDef_Start" spiffworkflow:triggerDoctype="Error Log" spiffworkflow:triggerType="After Insert">
        <bpmn:condition xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">error and method not in (&#34;ErrorLogTicketAgent&#34;, &#34;Error in ErrorLogTicketAgent scheduler task.&#34;, &#34;Error log Job Agent - Failed to cleanup session&#34;) and not method.startswith(&#34;BPMN &#34;)</bpmn:condition>
      </bpmn:conditionalEventDefinition>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="triage" name="Triage: Kill Switch + Exact Dedup" spiffworkflow:serverScript="Error Log Agent - Triage" spiffworkflow:scriptType="Server Script" spiffworkflow:scriptName="Error Log Agent - Triage">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads the AI Agent Configuration kill switch and, if enabled, checks open HD Tickets for an exact subject match on this error's title. Writes outcome (disabled|linked_duplicate|needs_ai) and, on needs_ai, the fields the AI task's prompt renders (error_title, error_details, existing_tickets_json).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_outcome" name="Outcome?" default="f5">
      <bpmn:incoming>f2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="end_disabled" name="Disabled (kill switch off)">
      <bpmn:incoming>f3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="end_duplicate" name="Linked - Duplicate">
      <bpmn:incoming>f4</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="ai_similarity_check" name="AI Agent Task: Similarity Check" spiffworkflow:serviceType="ai_agent" spiffworkflow:aiAgentConfig="Error Log Ticket Agent" spiffworkflow:aiBackend="direct_api" spiffworkflow:aiProvider="Anthropic" spiffworkflow:aiModel="claude-haiku-4-5-20251001" spiffworkflow:aiResponseFormat="json" spiffworkflow:aiResponseSchema="{&#34;type&#34;: &#34;object&#34;, &#34;required&#34;: [&#34;decision&#34;], &#34;properties&#34;: {&#34;decision&#34;: {&#34;type&#34;: &#34;string&#34;, &#34;enum&#34;: [&#34;match&#34;, &#34;no_match&#34;]}, &#34;ticket_name&#34;: {&#34;type&#34;: [&#34;string&#34;, &#34;null&#34;]}}}" spiffworkflow:aiOutputVariable="similarity_result" spiffworkflow:aiUserPrompt="New error:&#10;  title: {{ error_title }}&#10;  details: {{ error_details }}&#10;&#10;Existing open HD Tickets (JSON array of {name, subject, description}):&#10;{{ existing_tickets_json }}&#10;&#10;Respond with the JSON object your instructions specify.">
      <bpmn:documentation>system_prompt lives on the linked AI Agent Configuration record (authoritative at dispatch for a fresh, non-resumed call) — carries the full match/no_match instructions. This task only supplies the per-call data and the structured-output contract, fixing the old code's bug of always linking existing_tickets[0] on a match.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="apply_ai_result" name="Apply AI Result" spiffworkflow:serverScript="Error Log Agent - Apply AI Result" spiffworkflow:scriptType="Server Script" spiffworkflow:scriptName="Error Log Agent - Apply AI Result">
      <bpmn:documentation>decision=match links Error Log.hd_ticket to the AI-identified ticket_name; no_match creates a new HD Ticket (custom_ticket_category set — mandatory on the current schema; custom_is_doctype_related dropped — retired) and links it back.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>f6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="end_resolved" name="Ticket Resolved">
      <bpmn:incoming>f7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f1" sourceRef="start_error_logged" targetRef="triage" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f2" sourceRef="triage" targetRef="gw_outcome" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f3" name="Disabled" sourceRef="gw_outcome" targetRef="end_disabled">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression>outcome == "disabled"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f4" name="Exact match" sourceRef="gw_outcome" targetRef="end_duplicate">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression>outcome == "linked_duplicate"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f5" name="Needs AI" sourceRef="gw_outcome" targetRef="ai_similarity_check" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f6" sourceRef="ai_similarity_check" targetRef="apply_ai_result" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f7" sourceRef="apply_ai_result" targetRef="end_resolved" />
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_1" bpmnElement="error_log_ticket_triage_process">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="start_error_logged_di" bpmnElement="start_error_logged">
        <dc:Bounds x="152" y="182" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="130" y="225" width="80" height="27" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="triage_di" bpmnElement="triage">
        <dc:Bounds x="240" y="160" width="150" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_outcome_di" bpmnElement="gw_outcome" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="445" y="175" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="437" y="145" width="66" height="27" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="end_disabled_di" bpmnElement="end_disabled">
        <dc:Bounds x="552" y="42" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="522" y="10" width="96" height="27" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="end_duplicate_di" bpmnElement="end_duplicate">
        <dc:Bounds x="552" y="322" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="522" y="360" width="96" height="27" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="ai_similarity_check_di" bpmnElement="ai_similarity_check">
        <dc:Bounds x="640" y="160" width="150" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="apply_ai_result_di" bpmnElement="apply_ai_result">
        <dc:Bounds x="840" y="160" width="150" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="end_resolved_di" bpmnElement="end_resolved">
        <dc:Bounds x="1042" y="182" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="1020" y="225" width="80" height="27" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f1_di" bpmnElement="f1">
        <di:waypoint x="188" y="200" />
        <di:waypoint x="240" y="200" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f2_di" bpmnElement="f2">
        <di:waypoint x="390" y="200" />
        <di:waypoint x="445" y="200" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f3_di" bpmnElement="f3">
        <di:waypoint x="470" y="175" />
        <di:waypoint x="470" y="60" />
        <di:waypoint x="552" y="60" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="480" y="115" width="49" height="27" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f4_di" bpmnElement="f4">
        <di:waypoint x="470" y="225" />
        <di:waypoint x="470" y="340" />
        <di:waypoint x="552" y="340" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="480" y="265" width="66" height="27" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f5_di" bpmnElement="f5">
        <di:waypoint x="495" y="200" />
        <di:waypoint x="640" y="200" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="545" y="182" width="49" height="14" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f6_di" bpmnElement="f6">
        <di:waypoint x="790" y="200" />
        <di:waypoint x="840" y="200" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f7_di" bpmnElement="f7">
        <di:waypoint x="990" y="200" />
        <di:waypoint x="1042" y="200" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
